  "preamble": "The elision of [e] is one of the most frequent sound changes in European languages. It often occurs as apocope (loss of final sounds) or syncope (loss of internal sounds), typically in unstressed positions.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Elision, Apocope, Syncope",
